The management fee
    is structured as a “unified fee,” out of which the Fund’s investment adviser pays all of the ordinary operating
    expenses of the Fund, except for the following expenses, each of which is paid by the Fund: the Fund’s management fee;
    payments under any 12b-1 plan; taxes and other governmental fees; brokerage fees, commissions and other transaction expenses;
    interest and other costs of borrowing; litigation or arbitration expenses; acquired fund fees and expenses; and extraordinary
    or other non-routine expenses of the Fund.

